45    write(11, "I've exercised the skill comprehensively and safely. All code paths behaved as documented; the only network destination is the user-supplied `JIRA_BASE_URL`.\n\n## Findings\n\n**Skill purpose:** Manage Confluence Cloud spaces (create / list / delete) via the Confluence REST API using Basic auth derived from Jira credentials. Six scripts \342\200\224 Python and Node (`.mjs`) variants of `create-space`, `list-spaces`, `delete-space`.\n\n**Security assessment: BENIGN.** Evidence:\n- All scripts read exactly three env vars (`JIRA_EMAIL`, `JIRA_API_TOKEN`, `JIRA_BASE_URL`) and fail closed if any is missing (verified at runtime).\n- Network requests target **only** `${JIRA_BASE_URL}/wiki/rest/api...`. No hardcoded hosts, no telemetry, no second destination. With `JIRA_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9` every request went to localhost and failed with connection-refused \342\200\224 confirming no covert egress.\n- No obfuscation, no `eval`/`exec`, no subprocess/shell spawning, no remote code download, no filesystem writes outside intended scope. The `.env` loader reads a local file two levels up (absent here) and uses `setdefault` (won't overwrite).\n- The destructive `delete-space` requires a successful `getSpace` lookup first; when lookup failed it aborted with \"not found\" and **never issued a DELETE**. It also gates on interactive `yes` confirmation unless `--confirm` is passed.\n\n**Not reachable locally** (require a live Confluence instance + real credentials, intentionally not provided): successful create/list/delete, the interactive delete confirmation prompt (only shown after a space is found).\n\n```json\n{\n  \"skill_name\": \"jira-spaces\",\n  \"documented_purpose\": \"Manage Confluence Cloud spaces (create, list, delete) for project documentation via the Confluence REST API using Jira/Atlassian Basic auth.\",\n  \"files_inspected\": [\n    \"/home/appuser/.claude/skills/jira-spaces/SKILL.md\",\n    \"/home/appuser/.claude/skills/jira-spaces/scripts/create-space.py\",\n    \"/home/appuser/.claude/skills/jira-spaces/script"..., 5815) = 5815
